We noticed that multiple genes were identified in GTAs with multiple traits, leading us to examine potential horizontally pleiotropic genes. Of the 176 TWAS-prioritized genes, we identified 50 genes associated with multiple traits, many of which are genetically correlated (Supplementary Data 11). Nine genes showed >3 GTAs across different categories. For example, IDI1, a gene involved in cholesterol biosynthesis40, showed associations with three metabolic and two neuropsychiatric traits: body fat percentage (\documentclass[12pt]{minimal}
